Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::completion_status_parts_rebuild_the_status_field`.

The defect: `Completion::status_code_type` shifts the status field by 9 instead of 8, so it reads
bits 9 to 11. The generic code type of an ordinary failure still decodes as 0 when bits 8 to 11
are clear, but a command-specific failure (code type 1) reads as generic, and a set retry delay
bit leaks into the code type, so a driver matches the code against the wrong table.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(rebuilt, completion.status)`.

diff --git a/src/completion.rs b/src/completion.rs
--- a/src/completion.rs
+++ b/src/completion.rs
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@
     /// 7; 0 is [`STATUS_CODE_TYPE_GENERIC`].
     #[doc(alias = "SCT")]
     pub fn status_code_type(&self) -> u8 {
-        (self.status >> 8) as u8 & 0x7
+        (self.status >> 9) as u8 & 0x7
     }
 
